    {
      "parameters": {
        "fromEmail": "kevin@gadgetlesstech.com",
        "toEmail": "={{ $json.email }}",
        "subject": "What your keyword gap report is actually telling you",
        "emailType": "html",
        "message": "<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"></head><body style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#f5f5f5;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><div style=\"max-width:580px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;\"><div style=\"background:#000;padding:20px 28px;border-bottom:3px solid #00b8db;border-radius:8px 8px 0 0;\"><p style=\"margin:0;color:#00b8db;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:3px;text-transform:uppercase;\">Reading the Data</p><p style=\"margin:4px 0 0;color:#fff;font-size:18px;font-weight:900;font-style:italic;letter-spacing:-1px;\">SEO4GEO</p></div><div style=\"background:#fff;padding:32px 28px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;color:#333;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;\"><p>Hey {{ $json.name || 'there' }},</p><p>When you run an SEO4GEO audit, you are not just getting a list of keywords. You are getting a map of every search your competitors are winning that you are not even showing up for.</p><p>Here is how to read what you see:</p><table width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"margin:20px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f5f5f5;font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"color:#00b8db;font-weight:700;\">&#10003;</span> <strong>Keyword gaps</strong> &#8212; searches where your competitor ranks in the top 10 and you do not appear at all</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f5f5f5;font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"color:#00b8db;font-weight:700;\">&#10003;</span> <strong>Visibility score</strong> &#8212; your share of the total search demand in your market</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f5f5f5;font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"color:#00b8db;font-weight:700;\">&#10003;</span> <strong>Competitor advantage</strong> &#8212; the specific topics where they have authority and you do not</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f5f5f5;font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"color:#00b8db;font-weight:700;\">&#10003;</span> <strong>AI action plan</strong> &#8212; the fastest gaps to close based on your current rankings</td></tr></table><p>The number that usually surprises people most is the visibility score. Most local businesses are capturing less than 10% of the searches available to them in their market.</p><p>The other 90% is going to competitors &#8212; not because they have a better business, but because they have broader search coverage.</p><p>In the next email I will explain exactly why that gap exists and how it compounds over time.</p><table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"margin:24px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background:#00b8db;border-radius:6px;\"><a href=\"https://seo4geo.com/audit\" style=\"display:inline-block;padding:14px 28px;color:#000;font-size:13px;font-weight:900;text-decoration:none;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;\">View Your Audit &#8594;</a></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin:24px 0 0;\">&#8212; Kevin<br><span style=\"color:#999;font-size:13px;\">Gadgetlesstech</span></p><hr style=\"border:none;border-top:1px solid #eee;margin:28px 0;\"><p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#999;\">You received this because you signed up via SEO4GEO or the Gadgetlesstech Blueprint. <a href=\"#\" style=\"color:#00b8db;\">Unsubscribe</a></p></div></div></body></html>"
